{"_id":"68a7360d8ec3d8323af12784","nodeId":"rq_y_OBMD9AH_4aoecvAi","roadmapSlug":"backend","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:53.149Z","description":"# Transactions\n\nDatabase transactions are series of operations executed as atomic units to ensure data integrity. Follow ACID properties: Atomicity (all-or-nothing), Consistency (valid state), Isolation (no interference), Durability (permanent changes). Ensure reliable concurrent operations and data consistency.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"SQL Transactions Tutorial","url":"https://www.sqlservertutorial.net/sql-server-basics/sql-server-transaction/","_id":"6a7588bab0650226a5eb4542"},{"type":"video","title":"What is a Database transaction?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wHUOeXbZCYA","_id":"6a7588bab0650226a5eb4543"},{"type":"video","title":"ACID Properties in Databases With Examples","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GAe5oB742dw","_id":"6a7588bab0650226a5eb4544"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-07T07:26:50.654Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04ddfb5fcb94d041699c","title":"roadmap.sh - Master SQL","partner":"roadmap.sh","type":"course","url":"https://roadmap.sh/courses/sql"},{"_id":"6a5e04ddfb5fcb94d04169c5","title":"Scrimba - Backend Developer Career Path","partner":"Scrimba","type":"course","url":"http://scrimba.com/the-backend-developer-path-c0tbi0l98f?via=roadmap"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/backend/content/rq_y_OBMD9AH_4aoecvAi.md"}
